### [ ] 1 — CRIT: Fix Compiler Hang — `main.oo` expanded check never finishes (F26)

**In plain words:** The compiler freezes when checking the whole program. Small files pass fast. The big `main.oo` never prints `OK` or `ERR` — it just hangs until timeout. Build scripts hid this with `timeout 60 || true` and dropped the rest of the C code, so `check_function` disappeared downstream.

**Surface:** `ooda/oodac/check_drive.oo` (walk), `ooda/oodac/check_caps.oo` (`check_function` param scan + body `skip_balanced`), `ooda/oodac/parse_drive.oo` (`skip_balanced`), `ooda/oodac/load_import.oo` (expanded source), binary `ooda/oodac/oodac` (old, pre-guard).

**Repro (shell) — proves hang, not slow:**
```bash
timeout 5 ooda/oodac/oodac check ooda/oodac/main.oo > /tmp/main_out 2> /tmp/main_err; echo exit=$?
# observed: exit=124 empty (no OK/ERR, hang=FAIL per PROBE §0) — also timeout 70 still 124 after docs push
timeout 5 ooda/oodac/oodac check ooda/oodac/check_caps.oo > /tmp/cc_out 2> /tmp/cc_err; echo exit=$?
# isolated check_caps: exit=1 ERR field_at (fast) — hang only on expanded graph
```

**Root cause (from audit + PV2 + verify2 2026-08-12):**
- `check_caps.oo:37-92` param scan advanced `pos` for `COMMA`/`COLON`/`LBRACKET`/`RBRACKET` **without** `bracket_depth==0` guard — stray `]` left depth 0 and incorrectly granted `&Cap` (PV2 MED). `RPAREN` check at `:92` had no `pos<n` guard → `list_get OOB` abort 134 on truncated input, not fail-closed. `skip_balanced` progress not checked: `sb <= pos` could loop forever if `skip_balanced` returned same pos (old code before guard).
- `check_drive.oo:42-66` walk had no `iter` or `prev_pos` guard — `while pos<n` could spin if `check_function` returned same pos (old code). New guard added in `74f84a0` (`iter>n+100`, `pos==prev_pos` → `ERR hang guard`) but **not live** in old binary at `ooda/oodac/oodac` (mtime 11:43, pre-guard).
- `tokenize_lines` on expanded `main.oo` (imports concat → 1 MiB bound) is slow string code (audit F26 says 56.86s wall at `3fb94504`) — needs either cache warm (`.ooda-cache/check`) or modular `check_mod.oo` path. Current `p7_check_main_smoke.sh` expects <75s warm.

**What changed so far (74f84a0, not yet live in binary):**
- `check_caps.oo`: added `bracket_depth==0` for `RPAREN`/`LBRACE`/`COMMA`/`COLON`, `pos<n` guard before `RPAREN`, `sb<=pos` progress check for body/verify `skip_balanced` (now returns `pos+1` not loop).
- `check_drive.oo`: added `iter` + `prev_pos` hang guard with `ERR hang guard exceeded` / `no progress`.
- `check_cap_util.oo`: audit header for 16 net + 6 fs ops, `max_depth 32` bounded (verified, no hang).

**Fix still needed (owns):**
- **DE1 (Domain Expert 1) owns `ooda/oodac/check_caps.oo`** — keep `bracket_depth` guards, ensure no `import "token_fmt.oo"` (field_at is provided via `main.oo` expanded imports; isolated check should stay fast ERR, not pull whole graph). Verify `skip_until_semi` always `pos+1`.
- **DE2 (Domain Expert 2) owns `ooda/oodac/check_drive.oo` + `check_cap_util.oo`** — keep hang guard, ensure `tokenize_lines` not called twice (already single call after fix).
- **INT (Integration Tester) owns `ooda/scripts/oodac_pure_build*.sh` + rebuild** — rebuild `oodac` with `PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1 OODAC_BIN=./bootstrap/seed/oodac bash scripts/oodac_pure_build.sh oodac/main.oo /tmp/oodac_new` (seed does not hang), then `mv /tmp/oodac_new oodac/oodac`. This makes guard live.

**Validation — must be dual-repro (two clean shells, no pipe-masked `$?` per PROBE §7):**
```bash
timeout 5 /tmp/oodac_new check ooda/oodac/main.oo >out 2>err; echo exit=$?  # must be 0 or 1 with OK/ERR, not 124
timeout 70 /tmp/oodac_new check ooda/oodac/main.oo >out 2>err; echo exit=$?  # must finish <70s
bash ooda/scripts/p7_check_main_smoke.sh >out 2>err; echo exit=$?  # expect ALL OK (warm .ooda-cache)
bash ooda/scripts/ci_product.sh >out 2>err; echo exit=$?  # full product floor
grep -q "check_function" /tmp/oodac_new  # or nm | grep check_function — no silent drop
```

**Done when:** Both `timeout 5` and `timeout 70` finish with `OK` or `ERR` (not 124) dual-repro, `p7_check_main_smoke.sh ALL OK`, pure build no longer needs `|| true`.

